      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "THE MATH",
      "new_visual_element": "Expected against observed, typeset",
      "narration": "The whole method rests on one comparison. For every drug and every side effect, work out how many reports you would expect if the two had nothing to do with each other. That is the drug's total times the event's total, divided by the whole database. Then divide what you actually observed by that expected count.",
      "narration_text": "The whole method rests on one comparison. For every drug and every side effect, work out how many reports you would expect if the two had nothing to do with each other. That is the drug's total times the event's total, divided by the whole database. Then divide what you actually observed by that expected count.",
