      "act": "THE CONTRAST",
      "new_visual_element": "How much of the crude ratio survives shrinkage",
      "narration": "Now take two pairs from the actual run. Warfarin and gastrointestinal bleeding: 62 reports where fewer than three were expected. After shrinkage, 99 percent of that ratio survives. Then esculin and heart sounds: 16 reports where almost none were expected, a crude ratio above 55,000. After shrinkage, 4 percent survives. The method never asked how big the ratio was. It asked how much was standing behind it.",
